# Cloudflare Pages redirect map, for the knoxvilledsa.org apex cutover.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The apex has served WordPress for years, so its URLs are
# in Google's index, in members' bookmarks, in old Facebook posts and on printed
# material. Cutting the apex over to this site without a map turns every one of
# them into a 404. The staging host (new.knoxvilledsa.org) never needed this:
# it is noindexed and has no history, which is why the earlier decision to
# "accept the 404s" was correct THERE and is not correct here.
#
# SOURCE OF THE LEFT-HAND COLUMN. Every path below was read from the live
# WordPress sitemap on 2026-07-26 (wp-sitemap.xml and its children), not guessed.
# If WordPress gains pages before the cutover, re-read that sitemap.
#
# TRAILING SLASHES. WordPress publishes and indexes the slashed form
# ("/calendar/"); this site is built with trailingSlash:'never' and
# build.format:'file', so it serves the bare form ("/events"). Both forms are
# listed on the left so an old link works whichever way it was written down.
#
# HOSTNAME MATCHING. Pages matches on PATH ONLY. The www-to-apex redirect
# cannot live in this file; it is a zone-level Redirect Rule plus a proxied
# placeholder DNS record for www. See APEX_CUTOVER_RUNBOOK.md.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALL THREE of the originally unresolved pages now have homes (2026-07-27):
#
#   /members/ and /bylaws-revision/    -> /documents
#   /resources-for-our-discussion/     -> /resources, a real page built from the
#                                         old one's reading list
#
# See stack/commons/public/scripts/sync-documents.py for how /documents is
# generated and gated on the Records Index audience level.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

